    {
      "id": "fashion-pleat-fold",
      "topicId": "fashion",
      "sourceOrder": 44,
      "cycle": 1,
      "status": "READY_FOR_SAME_READER_FINAL",
      "literalGroups": [
        {
          "group": "prompt_ordered_answers_key",
          "literal": {
            "prompt": "Как называется перегиб ткани, образованный удвоением материала поверх самого себя, в отличие от застроченного сужающегося сгиба?",
            "answers": [
              "Вытачка",
              "Годе",
              "Ластовица",
              "Складка"
            ],
            "correctIndex": 3
          },
          "literalSHA256": "c1e8ce3edb1118b078997bbd3774d4e5ca9abfd85796c33d99abf55cafc0c6e4",
          "primaryGround": "PLEAT noun L62-L65 defines the fold as cloth material doubled over itself. The prompt explicitly contrasts DART3 L73 (stitched tapering fold), excluding the previously overlapping option. GODET L38 and GUSSET L40 define different seam-insert constructions.",
          "sourcePaths": [
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17c8c/source-fashion41/merriam-webster-fashion-terms.json",
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17c8c/source-fashion42/godet-context.json"
          ],
          "locator": "pleat L62-L65; dart L69-L74; godet L31-L38; gusset L31-L40",
          "sourcePathsBeforeTechnicalNormalization": [
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17c8c/source-fashion41/merriam-webster-fashion-terms.json",
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17c8c/source-fashion42/godet-context.json"
          ]
        },
        {
          "group": "explanation",
          "literal": "Складка — тканевый перегиб, образованный удвоением материала поверх самого себя. Вытачка — застроченный сужающийся сгиб; годе и ластовица — вставки в шов, отличающиеся назначением.",
          "literalSHA256": "449b7be074d743e4f4bc1cc644bb192151d10d13255c84bcdfa28d5bcc6eca13",
          "primaryGround": "The first sentence follows PLEAT L64. The second distinguishes the formerly overlapping dart using DART3 L73, then identifies godet and gusset as separate seam-insert forms (GODET L38; GUSSET L40).",
          "sourcePaths": [
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17c8c/source-fashion41/merriam-webster-fashion-terms.json",
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17c8c/source-fashion42/godet-context.json"
          ],
          "locator": "pleat L62-L65; dart L69-L74; godet L31-L38; gusset L31-L40",
          "sourcePathsBeforeTechnicalNormalization": [
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17c8c/source-fashion41/merriam-webster-fashion-terms.json",
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17c8c/source-fashion42/godet-context.json"
          ]
        },
        {
          "group": "note0",
          "literal": "Вытачка — застроченный сужающийся сгиб ткани в одежде.",
          "literalSHA256": "4c81fe4e4298b739ed27a5968e9cca2d007e62c15d23842ba6235cc5c70c2743",
          "primaryGround": "Merriam-Webster defines garment dart as a stitched tapering fold.",
          "sourcePaths": [
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17c8c/source-fashion41/merriam-webster-fashion-terms.json"
          ],
          "locator": "dart L69-L74",
          "sourcePathsBeforeTechnicalNormalization": [
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17c8c/source-fashion41/merriam-webster-fashion-terms.json"
          ]
        },
        {
          "group": "note1",
          "literal": "Годе — тканевая вставка, которую помещают в шов, чтобы придать изделию полноту.",
          "literalSHA256": "3bfbb634babb4c1d62d1854839651b6e290853f8073f02f0f75dc34aa6ec28a1",
          "primaryGround": "Merriam-Webster defines godet as cloth inset placed in a seam to give fullness.",
          "sourcePaths": [
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17c8c/source-fashion42/godet-context.json"
          ],
          "locator": "godet L31-L38",
          "sourcePathsBeforeTechnicalNormalization": [
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17c8c/source-fashion42/godet-context.json"
          ]
        },
        {
          "group": "note2",
          "literal": "Ластовица — вставка в шве, обычно треугольная или ромбовидная, для расширения или укрепления.",
          "literalSHA256": "a8f4ef6aedd3ea55eb91a0b895c5ace541412738cb25fbc5ca3b3cb134d68559",
          "primaryGround": "Merriam-Webster defines gusset as a usually triangular or diamond-shaped seam insert for expansion or reinforcement.",
          "sourcePaths": [
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17c8c/source-fashion41/merriam-webster-fashion-terms.json"
          ],
          "locator": "gusset L31-L40",
          "sourcePathsBeforeTechnicalNormalization": [
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17c8c/source-fashion41/merriam-webster-fashion-terms.json"
          ]
        },
        {
          "group": "note3",
          "literal": "Английский глагол pleat означает укладывать материал в складки; существительное впервые засвидетельствовано в XV веке.",
          "literalSHA256": "10672afa7b865056af3ee582ac92557a190bcd8bf9593286200c49461a5ed654",
          "primaryGround": "Merriam-Webster defines the verb pleat as arranging in pleats and dates the first known noun use to the 15th century.",
          "sourcePaths": [
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17c8c/source-fashion41/merriam-webster-fashion-terms.json"
          ],
          "locator": "pleat L42-L50; L109-L117",
          "sourcePathsBeforeTechnicalNormalization": [
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17c8c/source-fashion41/merriam-webster-fashion-terms.json"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "fourFullPromptAnswerNoteAssessments": [
